ar he was too tired and didn't want to traverse a lot. So he wanted to visit each of these n cities at least once with smallest possible traverse. Persian cities are connected with bidirectional roads. You can go from any city to any other one using these roads and there is a unique path between each two cities.\n\nAll cities are numbered 1 to n . Shapur is currently in the city 1 and he wants to visit all other cities with minimum possible traverse. He can finish his travels in any city.\n\nHelp Shapur find how much He should travel.\n\n## Input\n\nFirst line contains a single natural number n ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 5 ) ΓÇö the amount of cities.\n\nNext n ΓÇë-ΓÇë1 lines contain 3 integer numbers each x i , y i and w i ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë x i ,ΓÇë y i ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ,ΓÇë0ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë w i ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë2ΓÇë├ùΓÇë10 4 ). x i and y i are two ends of a road and w i is the length of that road.\n\n## Output\n\nA single integer number, the minimal length of Shapur's travel.\n\nPlease, do not use %lld specificator to read or write 64-bit integers in C++. It is preffered to use cout (also you may use %I64d ).\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n3\n1 2 3\n2 3 4\n```\n```\n7\n```","type":"text"}],"contestId":61,"index":"D","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Eternal Victory","problemKey":"61-D","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"2 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/61/problem/D"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]}