man army has one special trait ΓÇö powers of all the people in it are distinct.\n\nHelp Shapur find out how weak the Romans are.\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line of input contains a single number n ( 3ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 6 ) ΓÇö the number of men in Roman army. Next line contains n different positive integers a i ( 1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë i ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë n ,ΓÇë1ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë a i ΓÇëΓëñΓÇë10 9 ) ΓÇö powers of men in the Roman army.\n\n## Output\n\nA single integer number, the weakness of the Roman army. \n\nPlease, do not use %lld specificator to read or write 64-bit integers in C++. It is preffered to use cout (also you may use %I64d ).\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n3\n3 2 1\n```\n```\n1\n```","type":"text"}],"contestId":61,"index":"E","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Enemy is weak","problemKey":"61-E","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"5 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/61/problem/E"}],"schemaVersion":1}
